# Items
# Hot air balloon
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_crate.name = Hot air balloon crate
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_crate.description = Deploys a giant hot air balloon. Needs a clear space of 25 x 25 x 40 blocks.
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_basic_crate.name = Small hot air balloon crate
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_basic_crate.description = Deploys a small one-person hot air balloon. Needs a clear space of 7 x 14 x 7 blocks.
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_transport_crate.name = Animal transport balloon crate
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_transport_crate.description = Deploys a hot air balloon for a pilot and one passenger, with an iron cage hanging under the basket. Needs a clear space of 23 x 41 x 23 blocks.
orbis_horizon.items.cage_lever.name = Cage lever
orbis_horizon.items.cage_lever.description = Lever of the animal transport balloon. Pull it to lower the cage (balloon in the air, side closed), to raise it, or to stop it while it moves.
orbis_horizon.items.cage_gate_lever.name = Cage gate lever
orbis_horizon.items.cage_gate_lever.description = Lever of the animal transport balloon. Pull it to open or close the front side of the cage, when the cage is still and its floor rests on the ground. Closing it captures the passive animals inside.
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_chain.name = Hot air balloon burner chain
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_chain.description = Pull it to take off. Pull it again in flight to stop and set the balloon down where it is.
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_burner.name = Hot air balloon burner
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_burner.description = Fuel tank of the balloon. Put wood or charcoal in it before taking off. A flame comes out of it while it has fuel. It burns in flight and may leave charcoal in its output.
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_large_burner.name = Large hot air balloon burner
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_large_burner.description = Reinforced burner built for the large hot air balloon. It is needed to craft the large balloon crate.
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_brazier.name = Hot air balloon brazier
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_brazier.description = Unused since the burner shows the flame itself. Can be deleted.
orbis_horizon.items.airship_cloudwork_crate.name = Cloudwork airship crate
orbis_horizon.items.airship_cloudwork_crate.description = Deploys the Cloudwork airship. Its thrusters run on the core of the Gobliterator. Needs a clear space of 11 x 17 x 31 blocks.
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_crate.name = Steamboat crate
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_crate.description = Deploys a paddle steamboat on the water. Aim at the water where the stern should be. Needs a clear space of 15 x 14 x 28 blocks.
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_skiff_crate.name = Skiff
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_skiff_crate.description = Deploys a small propeller boat on the water that you sail yourself. Aim at the water where the stern should be. Needs a clear space of 5 x 5 x 9 blocks.
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_skiff_crate_placed.name = Skiff crate
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_skiff_crate_placed.description = Use it to pack the skiff back into a crate, with the contents of its chest.
orbis_horizon.items.airship_helm.name = Helm
orbis_horizon.items.airship_helm.description = Use it from the pilot spot to set off, and again underway to stop.
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_paddle_wheel.name = Paddle wheel
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_paddle_wheel.description = A large paddle wheel for the side of a steamboat. It takes a lot of room.
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_propeller.name = Propeller
orbis_horizon.items.steamboat_propeller.description = A bronze propeller on the stern shaft of a small boat.
orbis_horizon.items.ship_wheel.name = Ship's wheel
orbis_horizon.items.ship_wheel.description = A goldenwood ship's wheel on its post, to decorate a deck or a harbour.
orbis_horizon.interactionHints.helmTakeOff = Press [{key}] to take the helm and take off
orbis_horizon.interactionHints.deskMap = Press [{key}] to choose a destination
orbis_horizon.interactionHints.chainTakeOff = Press [{key}] to pull the chain and take off
orbis_horizon.items.airship_engine.name = Engine
orbis_horizon.items.airship_engine.description = Engine under the fuel tank. It glows while the tank above it has fuel.
orbis_horizon.items.airship_fuel_tank.name = Fuel tank
orbis_horizon.items.airship_fuel_tank.description = Fuel tank of the engine. Put wood or charcoal in it before setting off. The engine burns fuel only while the vehicle moves or turns. It can leave charcoal in its output.
orbis_horizon.items.airship_burner_outlet.name = Airship burner outlet
orbis_horizon.items.airship_burner_outlet.description = Rear burner outlet that pushes the airship forward. Two of them are needed to build an airship.
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_public_burner.name = Transit balloon burner
orbis_horizon.items.hotair_balloon_public_burner.description = Burner of the transit balloons that run between stations. It has no fuel slot: the flame stays lit.
orbis_horizon.items.balloon_station_marker.name = Balloon station marker
orbis_horizon.items.balloon_station_marker.description = Brazier that marks a balloon station. It is part of the station and cannot be crafted.
orbis_horizon.items.balloon_station_brazier.name = Balloon station brazier
orbis_horizon.items.balloon_station_brazier.description = Brazier of a balloon station. Its flame does not burn and cannot be put out.
orbis_horizon.items.balloon_station_map.name = Station map
orbis_horizon.items.balloon_station_map.description = Map of a balloon station. Decoration only: it does not get in the way of the station master.
# Camping tent
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_crate.name = Small Tent (old crate)
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_crate.description = Right-click on the ground to pitch a tent with a bed and a campfire. The empty crate stays in your inventory.
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_crate_empty.name = Small Tent (old empty crate)
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_crate_empty.description = Right-click on your tent to pack it back into this crate.
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_big_crate.name = Large Tent (old crate)
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_big_crate.description = Right-click on the ground to pitch a large tent with two beds, two chests and a campfire. The empty crate stays in your inventory.
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_big_crate_empty.name = Large Tent (old empty crate)
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_big_crate_empty.description = Right-click on your tent to pack it back into this crate.
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_decor_ladder.name = Tent decor ladder
orbis_horizon.items.camping_tent_decor_ladder.description = Decoration for the large tent. It looks like a ladder but cannot be climbed. It is a thin solid panel that can block the way.
orbis_horizon.items.airship_inkwell.name = Inkwell
orbis_horizon.items.airship_inkwell.description = Inkwell. It has no collision, so it never blocks the way.
orbis_horizon.items.airship_chair.name = Chair
orbis_horizon.items.airship_chair.description = Chair. You can sit on it, and it has no collision.
orbis_horizon.items.airship_stool.name = Stool
orbis_horizon.items.airship_stool.description = Passenger seat. You can sit on it, and it has no collision.
# Chat messages sent by the plugin
orbis_horizon.chat.takeoff.chain = Takeoff! Pull the chain again to stop and set the balloon down where it is.
orbis_horizon.chat.takeoff.command = Takeoff! Pull the chain or use /orbishorizon balloon land to land.
orbis_horizon.chat.landed = Landing successful.
orbis_horizon.chat.stopped = Hot air balloon stopped. In the air, the burner keeps burning and, once empty, the balloon comes down on its own. Pull the chain to take off again.
orbis_horizon.chat.landFailedContinue = {error} The flight continues.
orbis_horizon.chat.seated = You are seated in the basket. You will be set down on landing.
orbis_horizon.chat.landedStandUp = The hot air balloon has landed, you can stand up.
orbis_horizon.chat.pilotDied = The pilot died: the hot air balloon is coming down to the ground on its own.
orbis_horizon.chat.pilotDiedTakeOver = The pilot died, you can take their place to continue your journey.
orbis_horizon.chat.pilotLeft = The pilot left the vehicle: the hot air balloon is coming down to the ground on its own.
orbis_horizon.chat.fuel.dryDescentStart = Burner empty: the hot air balloon is coming down to the ground on its own, you are seated. It will land when it touches the ground.
orbis_horizon.chat.fuel.dryLanded = Hot air balloon landed, burner empty. Add fuel to take off again.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.alreadyPiloting = You are already flying a hot air balloon.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.notPiloting = You are not flying a hot air balloon.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.prefabUnreadable = The hot air balloon prefab cannot be read: {error}
orbis_horizon.chat.error.noPosition = Your position is unknown.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.noBalloon = No placed hot air balloon found around you. Get into the basket.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.noBurner = Burner not found. This hot air balloon may come from an older version of the mod: place a new one with a crate.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.burnerEmpty = The burner is empty. Put fuel (wood, planks, charcoal...) in the burner, the pipe above the chain, then try again.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.balloonFull = This balloon carries {max, plural, one {1 person} other {{max} people}} at most, the pilot included. Have {extra, plural, one {1 player} other {{extra} players}} get off, then try again.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.movement = The player's movement cannot be changed.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.modelMissing = Model {model} not found. The blocks have been put back.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.unknownModel = Unknown model: {model}
orbis_horizon.chat.error.noRoom = Not enough room here to set the hot air balloon down.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.groundCage = The balloon is coming down onto its cage. Wait for it to land.
orbis_horizon.chat.despawn.none = No hot air balloon within {radius} blocks.
orbis_horizon.chat.despawn.chunks = Part of the hot air balloon is outside the loaded chunks. Move closer.
orbis_horizon.chat.despawn.alreadyLanding = This hot air balloon is already landing.
orbis_horizon.chat.despawn.done = Hot air balloon removed. Its contents dropped to the ground, the crate is in your inventory.
orbis_horizon.chat.despawn.doneInventoryFull = Hot air balloon removed. Its contents and the crate dropped to the ground (inventory full).
orbis_horizon.chat.despawn.removedByAdmin = The hot air balloon was removed by an administrator.
orbis_horizon.chat.lock.balloon.break = This hot air balloon is locked: its blocks can't be removed.
orbis_horizon.chat.lock.balloon.place = This hot air balloon is locked: blocks can't be placed on it or in the basket.
orbis_horizon.chat.lock.tent.break = This tent is locked: its blocks can't be removed.
orbis_horizon.chat.lock.tent.place = This tent is locked: blocks can't be placed on it or inside it.
orbis_horizon.chat.lock.station.break = This station is locked: its blocks can't be removed.
orbis_horizon.chat.lock.station.place = This station is locked: blocks can't be placed on it or inside it.
orbis_horizon.chat.lock.boatStation.break = This boat station is locked: its blocks can't be removed.
orbis_horizon.chat.lock.boatStation.place = This boat station is locked: blocks can't be placed on it or inside it.
orbis_horizon.chat.tent.noRoom = Not enough room for the tent.
orbis_horizon.chat.tent.packUnreadable = The contents of this pack cannot be read, so it stays closed.
orbis_horizon.chat.error.heightLimit = The hot air balloon cannot be set down here: part of it would go beyond the height limit of the world.
orbis_horizon.chat.heightLimit.reached = The height limit of the world is reached: the vehicle cannot go any further.
orbis_horizon.chat.deploy.heightLimit = Not enough height here: part of the structure would go beyond the height limit of the world. Nothing was placed.
orbis_horizon.chat.deploy.underwater = This cannot be set up under water: move to dry land.
orbis_horizon.chat.deploy.stationZone = Too close to the {station} quay, set down further away.
orbis_horizon.chat.gameMode.left = You left the vehicle because your game mode changed.
orbis_horizon.chat.tent.aimTent = Aim at a pitched tent.
orbis_horizon.chat.tent.notOwner = Only the player who pitched this tent can pack it.
orbis_horizon.chat.tent.approach = Move closer to the tent.
orbis_horizon.chat.tent.packed = Tent packed.
orbis_horizon.chat.tent.packedDropped = Tent packed. Its contents dropped to the ground.
orbis_horizon.chat.tent.packedKept = Tent packed. Its contents are in the crate.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.crouchToPitch = Crouch to pitch your camp.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.packed = Camp packed.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.packedKept = Camp packed. Your belongings are inside the pack.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.packInChest = A camping pack cannot be stored inside a tent. It was dropped on the ground.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.droppedAtFeet = Camp packed. Your inventory is full, the pack fell at your feet.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.notOwner = Only the player who pitched this camp can pack it.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.bagBlocked = The bag of this camp is blocked by another block. Use /orbishorizon camping pack near it to pack the camp.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.noneNearby = No camp within reach.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.respawnForgotten = This wake-up spot is forgotten.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.respawnNotFound = No camp wake-up spot of yours here.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.approach = Move closer to the camp.
orbis_horizon.chat.camp.notACamp = This is not a camp you can pack.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.learned = You learned to craft {name}. Furniture bench.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.added = Added to your journal: {name}.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.known = {name} is already in your journal.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.newPage = New page in your journal: {family}.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.titleEarned = Title earned: {title}
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.nothing = Nothing to note about this block.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.disabled = Furniture discovery is disabled on this server.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.lost_civilization.name = Lost civilisation
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.lost_civilization.lore = Long before the first villages, a people built in stone and dark wood. Only moss-covered ruins remain, doors that lead nowhere and faceless statues. Every piece of furniture you find is part of the puzzle.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.village.name = Village
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.village.lore = The villages of Orbis live by the rhythm of harvests and markets. Their furniture is plain and sturdy, built to last for generations. Villagers gladly let a traveller sit at their table.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Bed = The frame held, the mattress turned to dust long ago.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Brazier = The ashes at the bottom have been cold for centuries.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Chair = A council chair, perhaps. It is still waiting for someone.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Chest_Small = Empty, but the lock was forced from the inside.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Door = The wood has swollen, the door no longer quite shuts.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Ladder = The rungs are worn in the middle by thousands of steps.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Sign = The letters are gone. No one knows what it once announced.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Stool = Still sturdy enough to sit on.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Table = Regular notches on the top. A tally, or a calendar.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Wardrobe = A scent of cedar still lingers inside.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Window = You could see the sky through it, and you still can.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Banner = The emblem has faded, but the gold thread still shines.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Banner_Double = Two banners for two allied houses.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Banner_Triple = Three banners side by side. A hall of some importance.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Bench = A bench of stone and wood where people waited to be received.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Bookshelf = The books are unreadable, but someone sorted them by size.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Candle = The wax ran down to the floor and set.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Coffin = The lid bears a carved name no one can read any more.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Desk = Ink stains on the wood. Someone wrote a lot here.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Door_Large = A door made to impress those who walked through it.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Door_Medium = Wide enough for a cart, if you push hard.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Lantern = The glass is cracked, the wick only needs a spark.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Lantern_Ceiling = It lit a hall where people talked loud and long.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Planter = The original plants are gone, others took their place.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Platform = A dais. Someone stood here to be seen.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Pot = A layer of fossilised grain still clings to the sides.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Pot_Small = Small enough to hold in one hand, tough enough to have survived.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Shelf = Rings in the dust show where jars once stood.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Statue = A faceless guardian, still facing the entrance.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Statue_Broken = The head is missing. It was never found.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Torch = The bracket was set into the stone to last.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Human_Ruins_Trapdoor = It opens onto a stairway no one has gone down in a long time.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Bed = A plain bed and a thick blanket, and sleep comes on its own.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Brazier = People warm their hands at it on market evenings.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Painting_1x1 = A small portrait of an ancestor, hung by the door.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Bench = The bench where the elders comment on passing travellers.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Bookcase = Almanacs, recipes and a single novel the whole village has read.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Coffin = The carpenter always keeps one ready. You never know.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Painting_1x2 = A landscape of hills, painted by a passing traveller.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Painting_2x1 = A harvest scene in ochres and yellows.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Painting_2x2 = The village as it was a hundred years ago. Not much has changed.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Painting_3x2 = The great founding mural, a gift from the first mayor.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Pot = It still smells of yesterday's soup.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Statue = The village hero. No one agrees on what the hero actually did.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Village_Tombstone = Fresh flowers lie at the foot of the stone.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.lost_civilization.title = Ruin archaeologist
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.village.title = Friend of the villages
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.feran.name = Feran
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.feran.lore = The Feran build close to the ground, with pale wood, rope and stretched hide. Their homes smell of smoke and dried herbs. Everything looks made to be moved quickly, yet mended with great care.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.feran.title = Friend of the Feran
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Bench = The wood is polished smooth by generations of evening conversation.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Bookshelf = Tied scrolls, filed in an order only the owner understands.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Door = A taut flap of hide. It keeps the wind out, not the curious.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Ladder = Every rung is knotted by hand, never twice the same way.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Platform = A light platform, meant to be taken apart before the next move.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Pot = A round pot etched with spirals. It still smells of bitter herbs.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Pot_Secondary = Smaller than its twin but far more worn. It was clearly used every day.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Shelf = Three planks, a few cords, and room enough for a whole camp.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Sign = Symbols painted in haste. They mark a path, or perhaps a warning.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Stool = A low stool, ideal for watching the fire without tiring.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Table = The knife marks form a map, or perhaps a game.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Trapdoor = It hides a food store. The neighbours are not supposed to know.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Wardrobe = Folded hides, festival feathers and a scent of cedar.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Feran_Window = A narrow opening, turned east to watch for the first light.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.scarak_temple.name = Primordial Scarak temple
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.scarak_temple.lore = Before the hives, the Scarak raised temples of ochre stone in the desert. The halls are narrow, the ceilings low, the patterns repeated endlessly. You feel watched by something very old.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.scarak_temple.title = Sand delver
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Brazier = A blackened stone bowl. Someone tended this fire before the hives existed.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Chest_Small = A small stone chest, carved with lines so fine you feel them more than see them.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Door_Large = It opens onto a hall where no one entered uninvited.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Door_Medium = The hinges still hold a little sand, as if it were opened yesterday.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Ladder = The grips are cut into the stone, sized more for claws than hands.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Lamp = An amber glow still sleeps inside, patient as the stone.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Lantern = Hung from the ceiling, it lit ceremonies of which only echoes remain.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Planter = A stubborn plant grows in the planter's sand, watered by no one.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Platform = A raised slab, worn in the middle by those who stood there to pray.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Pot = The thick walls keep a cellar's coolness, even in the open desert.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Secondary_Pot = Another pot, flatter. Perhaps seeds were left in it as offerings.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Statue = An angular face, many arms, and a gaze that follows every visitor.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Scarak_Window = A slit cut to let through exactly one ray of sun at noon.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.kweebec.name = Kweebec
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.kweebec.lore = The Kweebec live deep in the forests, in houses of living wood and leaves. Their furniture is small, round and a little crooked. There is more curiosity than rigour in it, and that suits it well.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.kweebec.title = Kweebec companion
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Door = Low and round, it makes every visitor bow on the way in.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Ladder = The rungs are barely stripped branches, still a little green.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Painting = An understorey landscape painted with great affection and little perspective.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Platform = A platform in the branches, for watching the clouds go by in peace.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Shelf = Dried mushrooms, seeds, and a pebble kept for no particular reason.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Sign = An arrow and a drawn leaf. Impossible to tell where it leads.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Statue = A tiny carved figure whose smile is slightly too wide for its face.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Stool = A barely worked stump. You sit on it and swing your feet.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Table = It leans to one side, and no one ever thought to straighten it.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Trapdoor = A moss-covered trapdoor. You only see it if you look for it.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Wardrobe = Capes of woven leaves, hung neatly in order of season.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Kweebec_Window = A round opening where a bird has clearly made its nest.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.royal_magic.name = Royal magic
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.royal_magic.lore = In the Grand Wizard's drawing rooms, everything seems to hum with a held breath. The fabrics are too rich, the gold too polished, the shadows a little too long. Here, even an armchair keeps a secret.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.royal_magic.title = Court familiar
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Royal_Magic_Bed = The silk sheets never crease. No one seems ever to have slept here.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Royal_Magic_Chair = A high back, carved arms. You feel judged the moment you sit.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Royal_Magic_Couch = A couch far too soft, where advisers must have dozed during audiences.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Royal_Magic_Medium_Door = It swings open by itself if you hesitate in front of it long enough.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Royal_Magic_Pot = A thin violet wisp sometimes rises from the neck, then vanishes.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Royal_Magic_Table = Rings of wax and ink mark the top. Spells were prepared here.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Royal_Magic_Wardrobe = Robes embroidered with stars. One of them stirs when you look away.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.light_temple.name = Light temple
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.light_temple.lore = The temples of light are built to catch every last ray. Their pale stones hold the day's warmth well into the night. You walk quietly there, as in a place that has not finished praying.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.light_temple.title = Keeper of the light
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Light_Bed = A pale slab, hollowed in the centre. Offerings were laid here at dawn.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Light_Bench = A long bench where the faithful waited, eyes closed, for the sun to find them.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Light_Door_Large = Each morning it opened to the east to let in the first light.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Light_Door_Medilum = The golden lines on the leaf form a half-faded sun.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Light_Painting = A sky painted upside down, the sun at the bottom. Perhaps a prayer.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Light_Platform = You climbed here to receive the light before anyone else. A coveted honour.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Light_Pot = It held clear water, changed daily by a forgotten ritual.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Light_Statue = Eyes closed, hands open. You lower your voice near it without knowing why.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.ancient.name = Ancient age
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.ancient.lore = Objects from this age have outlived so many centuries that the wood has turned the colour of ash. Nobody knows who made them or why they were left behind. In cellars and crypts you still find frozen gestures, a sack set down, a torch ready to be lit.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.ancient.title = Keeper of ages
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Ancient_Barrel = The hoops have rusted through, yet the barrel still rings hollow when you knock.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Ancient_Coffin = The lid has slipped a finger's width. Someone wanted to check, or to get out.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Ancient_Crate = The planks split outwards, as if the loading had been done in too much of a hurry.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Ancient_Painting = Only a horizon and two small figures survive. The rest flaked away with the paint.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Ancient_Pot = The neck is chipped, but the belly still carries a pattern of spirals.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Ancient_Sack = Nothing inside but a single grain of wheat, hard as a pebble.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Ancient_Statue = The face is smooth, yet the hands stayed sharp. They hold something that is no longer there.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Ancient_Torch = The pitch at the tip is cracked. A single spark of flint might be enough.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.scarak_hive.name = Scarak hive
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.scarak_hive.lore = In the hive, everything is tunnel, resin and a distant hum. The walls seep a warm glow, and every corner has its purpose. This world is shaped for a colony, not for a lone traveller.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.scarak_hive.title = Hive scout
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Scarak_Hive_Door_Large = It closes slowly behind you, like a jaw taking its time.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Scarak_Hive_Door_Medium = Dry fibres hold it together. It creaks whenever the colony passes.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Scarak_Hive_Ladder = A thick vine lines the wall. It holds a surprising amount of weight.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Scarak_Hive_Lamp = The larva pulses gently, as if dreaming out loud.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Scarak_Hive_Lantern = Hung on a silk thread, it lights a corridor no one sweeps any more.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Scarak_Hive_Platform = Layers of pressed wax form this floor, sticky in places.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Scarak_Hive_Window = An uneven opening, gnawed rather than cut, letting in warm air.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.dark_temple.name = Dark temple
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.dark_temple.lore = The dark temple keeps its corridors in a night that never loosened its grip. Outlanders left stone deities and candles that barely light anything. You walk in with a low voice and the feeling of being watched.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.dark_temple.title = Pilgrim of the dark
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Dark_Candle = The flame never flickers, as if the air of the temple held its breath.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Dark_Coffin = Narrower than a village coffin. Whoever lay here may not have been quite like us.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Dark_Door_Large = It opens inwards, as if to stop something from getting out.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Dark_Door_Medium = The threshold is worn by slow steps, all going the same way.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Dark_Pot = A jar sealed with black wax. You do not shake it.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Dark_Statue = The eyes follow whoever passes. It might be the light, and you prefer to think so.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Dark_Statue_Gaia = A deity of the Outlanders, arms spread. A welcome or a warning, the notebook cannot tell.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.frozen_castle.name = Frozen castle
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.frozen_castle.lore = Somewhere in the north a castle sleeps under a crust of ice as thick as a hand. Its halls stayed in order, as if everyone left within the hour. The frost preserved everything, down to the last breath you almost see hanging in the air.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.frozen_castle.title = Frostbound traveller
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Frozen_Castle_Bed = The sheets have become a sheet of ice. The hollow of a sleeper remains all the same.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Frozen_Castle_Bench = A line of frost in the shape of people sitting, or so it looks when you stare long enough.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Frozen_Castle_Lamp = The flame has been sealed in its glass so long it almost looks made of ice.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Frozen_Castle_Pot = A vase split by frost, its two halves held together by the ice.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Frozen_Castle_Secondary_Lamp = A twin lantern on the far side of the hall, so no one walked in the dark.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Frozen_Castle_Secondary_Pot = Another vase, smaller, still full of water turned to crystal.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.jungle.name = Jungle
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.jungle.lore = In the jungle everything grows faster than you can build, so people build in bamboo. Huts are light, ropes are taut, the air is heavy with warm rain. Each piece smells of fresh cane, and one storm is enough for the vines to take it back.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.jungle.title = Vine walker
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Jungle_Bookshelf = The scrolls are tied with strips of vine. Damp has reached nearly all of them.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Jungle_Brazier = The embers are covered with green leaves, so the smoke keeps mosquitoes away.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Jungle_Painting = Parrots painted in berry juice, slightly smeared by the monsoon.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Jungle_Pot = A woven vase that keeps water cool, if you leave it in the shade.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Jungle_Pot_Secondary = A second, squatter vase, used as a store for seeds.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.wind_temple.name = Wind temple
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.wind_temple.lore = The wind temple stands where the air never rests. Its doors whistle, its vaults sing, and its statues seem to wait for one particular breath. You always hear someone else there, and it is almost never anyone.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.wind_temple.title = Breath seeker
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Wind_Door_Large = Its panels are pierced with small holes. It plays a note when the wind picks up.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Wind_Door_Medium = One hand opens it, but never quietly. It sings every time.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Wind_Pot = A narrow mouth and a wide belly. Blow across it and it answers.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Wind_Statue = A beast with vast wings, caught mid-leap. The wind always seems to come from it.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Wind_Statue_Gaia = A deity that says nothing. Oddest of all, the wind falls quiet around it.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.goblin.name = Goblin
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.goblin.lore = Goblins build with whatever they find, and they find a great deal. Their lairs smell of smoke, hot metal and suspicion. You soon learn to tell what was made there from what was simply taken from someone else.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.goblin.title = Lair plunderer
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Goblin_Coffer = A small coffer that seems to murmur when you step away. Best not to turn your back on it.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.crude.name = Crude
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.crude.lore = Before workshops and sawmills there were logs, rope and bare hands. These pieces were made in a hurry and for a short stay, yet they tell of lives that had nothing else. Each one carries its maker's fingerprints.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.crude.title = Makeshift builder
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Crude_Brazier = A ring of stones and embers still warm. The camp has only just emptied.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.emerald_temple.name = Overgrown temple
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.emerald_temple.lore = Somewhere beneath the vines, a green temple has slept for a very long time. Roots have lifted the flagstones and moss has eaten the names. You walk through it quietly, as though the statues were listening.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.emerald_temple.title = Green temple warden
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Emerald_Bed = Ferns grow where a head once rested. Someone kept a long vigil here.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Emerald_Door_Medium = A vine has crept into the frame. Whether it opens or holds the door shut, no one can say.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Temple_Emerald_Statue = A wooden figure with hollowed eyes. The moss has given it eyebrows.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.tavern.name = Tavern
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.tavern.lore = Somewhere along the road, a lantern marks a tavern. Inside there is a fire, a tankard and stories, half of them true. The furniture is marked by elbows, laughter and quarrels forgotten before dawn.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.tavern.title = Tavern regular
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Tavern_Barrel = It sounds hollow, which is rare on a market night. The landlord must be worried.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Tavern_Painting = A portrait of the house founder, far too flattering to be honest.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.desert.name = Desert
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.desert.lore = In the dunes, the wind wipes out footprints and hands ruins back to the sand. The furniture that surfaces is dry, cracked and oddly intact. You can tell its makers knew how to live under a merciless sun.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.desert.title = Dune wanderer
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Desert_Bed = Sand has crept into every fold. Whoever slept here left long ago.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.lumberjack.name = Lumberjack
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.lumberjack.lore = Deep in the forests, cabins stand beside fresh stumps. Lumberjacks live to the rhythm of axe and fire, with furniture cut from the very wood they fell. Everything smells of sap and smoke.
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.family.lumberjack.title = Forest companion
orbis_horizon.chat.discovery.item.Furniture_Lumberjack_Painting = A carefully painted forest, hung by someone who never sees its end.
